      "label": "BetterAuth Session Cookie Authentication (Client Side)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "dev_docs/frontend-dev-guide.md",
      "source_location": "section 2",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Web relies on browser cookie handling via fetch credentials:'include'; mobile must persist and resend the better-auth.session_token cookie manually (expo-secure-store or BetterAuth RN client) because React Native has no cookie jar."
    },
    {
      "id": "dev_docs_frontend_dev_guide_nativewind_tailwind_stack",
      "label": "NativeWind v4 + Tailwind v3 Styling Stack",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "dev_docs/frontend-dev-guide.md",
      "source_location": "section 3",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Mobile deliberately pins NativeWind v4 with Tailwind v3 because the NativeWind + Tailwind v4 combination is not yet stable for production."
    },
    {
      "id": "dev_docs_frontend_dev_guide_primary_color_tokens",
      "label": "Primary Color Tokens (tailwind.config.js)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "dev_docs/frontend-dev-guide.md",
      "source_location": "section 3",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Design tokens (primary-50..primary-900, sky-blue scale) are centralized in apps/mobile/tailwind.config.js theme.extend so new colors are added in one place."
    },
    {
      "id": "dev_docs_frontend_dev_guide_shared_ui_package",
      "label": "@4sports/ui Shared Component Package",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "dev_docs/frontend-dev-guide.md",
      "source_location": "section 4",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Components in packages/ui affect web and mobile simultaneously, so the team rule is: check for an existing component before creating one, and coordinate (Ivan asks Garib) before adding new shared components."
    },
    {
      "id": "dev_docs_frontend_dev_guide_expo_router_navigation",
      "label": "Expo Router v4 File-Based Navigation",
      "file_type": "concept",
